From 9e1c69f3454639a00751f8ecedc22baa8efdd6df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:27:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09270/11362] It was the context budget, not the model: 6/6 at
 n_ctx 131072 against 0/5 at 65536

Two days of "Qwen3.8 fails to terminate" was the model hitting a wall I built.

THE PAIRED MATRIX (results/arc_qwen38_context_matrix_20260816/). Same game, same
prompt, same required symbols, same tries, same seeds, n_ctx 131072, --parallel 1:

  seed   model-card 0.6/0.95/20    shipped 0.2 ladder
  100    ok  1770s                 ok  1519s
  200    ok  1817s                 ok  2348s
  300    ok  2447s                 ok  1496s

6/6. Both sampling conditions, every seed. At n_ctx 65536 the same call was 0/5.
Sampling made NO difference to success and greedy was marginally faster, so Qwen's
endless-thinking-repetition warning does not apply here -- a refutation worth as
much as a confirmation, and considerably more than the guess I would have shipped.
The sampling override stays default-off; the arm carries no unmotivated difference.

THE ARM'S OWN ADDITIONS OVERFLOWED THE BUDGET. A plain induce call finishes in
~41.4k tokens -- measured at budgets of 49,152 and 114,688, which differ by 2.3x
and moved usage 0.5%. The arm's call (symbol directive + required symbols +
retries) needs ~58-63k; seed 100 used 57,932 against a 49,152 ceiling. I added
those to the prompt and never re-sized the budget underneath them.

--parallel 1 IS WHAT MAKES 131072 AFFORDABLE. llama-server defaulted to
n_parallel=4, so `-c` was divided four ways for a workload issuing one request at
a time. One slot doubled usable context for 1.3 GB: 9,752+10,574 MiB at 4x65536
versus 11,096+11,936 at 1x131072. Eighth borrowed constant, and the only free one.

AND THE RESERVE WAS FITTED TO ONE GAME. It was N_CTX-16384, sized against tu93's
15,846-token prompt because tu93 is what I probed. All 13 roster prompts, measured
with the model's own vocab:

  tr87 20,173  ft09 17,802  lp85 16,467  sk48 16,074  tu93 15,846
  r11l 12,672  re86 11,902  g50t 11,756  ar25 11,612  sb26 11,065
  cd82  7,688  vc33  7,452  sp80  5,492

THREE games exceed 16,384 -- tr87 by 3,789. On those the requested n_predict was
larger than the room actually left, so generation was truncated by the pool rather
than by its own budget: a spurious overrun indistinguishable in the shard from a
real one. That is the same defect as the headline finding, one level down, and it
would have survived the fix if I had sized the new reserve from tu93 again.

PROMPT_RESERVE = 28672 (largest + ~8k margin) -> 102,400 tokens to answer in.

Evidence preserved rather than described: the six matrix cells, the two plain-call
probes at different budgets, and the per-game prompt census.
